{"tool_name":"peako","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:peako"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"peaKO","home":"https://peako.hoffmanlab.org","summary":"Motif elucidation in ChIP-seq datasets with a knockout control | PeaKO discovers motifs in ChIP-seq datasets with knockout controls. PeaKO takes in paired wild-type/knockout BAM files in addition to several reference files, as input. It returns a file of ranked motifs (see our paper for more details) | PeaKO finding transcription factor binding motifs using knockout controls | Denisko D, Viner C, Hoffman MM. Motif elucidation in ChIP-seq datasets with a knockout control. BioRxiv 10.1101/721720 [Preprint]. 2019. Available from: https://doi.org/10.1101/721720 | PeaKO identifies motifs relevant to ChIP-seq experiments by combining two differential analysis approaches. It often improves elucidation of the target motif over other methods and highlights the benefits of knockout controls","addition_date":"2019-11-14T18:13:45Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:37:51.574436Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:peaKO","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"},{"term":"Sequence motif discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0238"},{"term":"Transcription factor binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0445"}]}],"name":"peaKO","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioadv/vbad031","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/721720","type":["Preprint"]}],"topic":[{"term":"ChIP-on-chip","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3179"},{"term":"ChIP-seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3169"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:peako/lib/peako.hoffmanlab.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/